1. Constitution (one short paper) — what IOX is
Paste/expand leaf 11 + one paragraph from leaf 4.
Lock: open, web, composable assets, surfaces, marketplace → ~local, offline, no window-island custody.
Audience: humans + machines. Length: ≤ 1 screen.

2. Composition law (the B-chain for Pocket) — how a surface works
The four moves, in pocket nouns:

1. Declare — surface.cfg (id, name, auth, dressup)
2. Rooms/slots — what belongs here (configs for bins/chips/tools)
3. Look — shell/style agency
4. Compose — available tools/kits only; no mega-desk reinvention

Include: desk is not root; runtime hosts surfaces.
Dossier/FileKeeper lesson: one jack, many rooms — don’t fork browsers into new products.

3. Boot & ownership — who owns what
┌───────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┐
│ Thing                     │ Owner                            │
├───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤
│ Process / void-mirror     │ IOX core (thin)                  │
├───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤
│ Auth shelf ~local/<user>/ │ user                             │
├───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤
│ surfaces/<Name>/          │ that surface                     │
├───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤
│ library/ materials        │ user (shared clay)               │
├───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤
│ ~host/marketplace         │ store / packs                    │
├───────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤
│ Tools on desk             │ surface placement + kit identity │
└───────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────┘

Boot options: default surface for this install (yours: Archivist) vs void first vs last-used. Document so “someone else installs” isn’t stuck in your desk myth.

4. Object dictionary (stable nouns)
chip / bin / board / book / tool / surface / kit / dressup / prop / pos — what each paper is, dual matter+cfg if that’s law.
No inventing Mail.* style freestyle.

5. What Pocket Desktop is in the fork
Honest inventory:

• Keep as DNA: multi-object felt, library+configs, spawn, dress, membership, stamper/inbox as guest tools, ROM window as interim tool surface
• Strip as product identity: DEFAULT_SURFACE = ArchivistDesk as universe
• Promote: surface list, enter/leave surface, void boot
• Out of scope for core: Dossier clones, full myPI letter alphabet, EDN cities

6. Tool = jack law (one page)
• Tools live as packages (~host / marketplace)
• Surfaces place instances
• Bigger “apps” (music ambient on save, file browse) = compose or extend jacks, not new monorepos
• Music example belongs in this doc as the ambient state pattern (same as Echo soundtrack)

7. Migration / fork map
pocket-desktop → iox-os (or name you choose):

• What moves (desk_sys hollow core, store paper law)
• What stays personal (your ArchivistDesk configs, leaves)
• What becomes sample surface pack
• What becomes marketplace kit

8. Anti-patterns (half page)
• Surface hard-coded as root
• Mega desk that reimplements tools
• Second FileKeeper
• Docs that are girl-weather leave-offs instead of instructionals
• Renaming without claim/compose behavior

───

Minimal set if you only write three

1. Leaf 11 polished = public constitution
2. Composition + boot/void = engineer law (this conversation + B-chain rhyme)
3. Object dictionary + jack law = so forks don’t invent nouns

Leaf 4 is appendix or “hollow core howl” for implementers.